  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1235 AM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThe first of two upper level ridges that will be in control of\nour weather for the next seven days is passing to the east while\nthe next ridge is building to the west. We are probably amid the\ndriest airmass we have seen in months. The 00z Nashville RAOB\nrecorded a column precipitable water of just 0.47 inches. \n\nThrough the week deep layer ridging builds in from the\nsouthwest. This keeps the dry airmass locked in place with\ngradual warming through the week. Highs work towards the mid to\nupper 70s. Deterministic GFS tries to flatten the ridge out\nearly next week, but ECMWF, ensembles and GFSAI/ECMWFAI do not\nseem to think we break from the pattern at that point.\nNevertheless an enjoyable and stable period of weather still\nlooks likely for the predictable future.",
